- It decodes the provided token with the same secret and algorithm at `auth/jwt.py:41`.
- If decoding fails for any reason, including expiration, invalid signature, malformed token, or wrong algorithm, it returns `None` at `auth/jwt.py:42-43`.
- It then requires `claims.get("typ") == "refresh"` at `auth/jwt.py:44-45`. So an access token cannot be passed to `refresh()`, because access tokens do not include `"typ": "refresh"`.
